WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:06.318
Before building booking experience, define the problem and the decision it will support.

2
00:00:06.318 --> 00:00:10.811
Make the expected outcome measurable, and record what is still an assumption.

3
00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:13.234
Map the booking journey in Miro.

4
00:00:13.234 --> 00:00:18.673
Ask Gemini to challenge the research assumptions, then record the evidence in Notion.

5
00:00:18.673 --> 00:00:23.415
Distinguish a customer problem from a feature that only sounds attractive.

6
00:00:23.815 --> 00:00:26.997
Translate the opportunity into a small experiment.

7
00:00:26.997 --> 00:00:31.769
Use Jira for acceptance criteria and Figma for the interaction hypothesis.

8
00:00:31.769 --> 00:00:36.414
Compare the proposal with the evidence before choosing the next release.

9
00:00:36.814 --> 00:00:41.197
Bring the evidence, cost, and next decision into validated product brief.

10
00:00:41.197 --> 00:00:45.701
The output is a shared direction, with clear ownership and a review point.
